  "briefing": "Two apartment blocks stand ten tiles apart in the camp quarter, with two of the people taken at First Light in each. I can place both doors and the guard on each, and nothing inside. Take out the guard on each door, and bring three of the four to the extraction on the north edge inside six minutes. Fewer than three is a loss. Anyone on the ground round either block warns the other inside twenty seconds, and their firing positions cover the lane between. A missile team on each roof looks into any yard you cross. So split and go in together, or take one and fight for the second. The second is slower, louder and dearer. Both blocks are lived in, and the one that holds the taken holds the neighbours as well. A cannon round into either is fourteen Conduct. Fifteen is the line. One hit on a block is fourteen, and a second hit ends the mission.",
  "aftermath": "Three came back from the camp quarter, or four, and the Marj counted each of them.",
  "debrief": {
    "victory": {
      "speaker": "idit",
      "text": "Three or four came back down the lane. Two houses were never meant to be taken at once, and the camp quarter has that to remember."
    },
    "defeat": {
      "speaker": "shai",
      "text": "Not today. The blocks are warned and the lane is covered, and the people in them are exactly where they were."
    }
  },
